      <gap reason="sampling"/>
      <div type="register">
        <head type="rubric">INCIPIUNT CAPITULA Libri primi.</head>
        <div type="registerItem" n="1">
          <head type="number">I.</head>
          <head type="rubric">Quod nulli sit ultima poenitentia deneganda.</head>
        </div>
        <div type="registerItem" n="2">
          <head type="number">II.</head>
          <head type="rubric">De his qui necessitate mortis urgente poenitentiam simul et Viaticum petunt: et de his qui
            obtumescunt antequam ad eos Sacerdos daturus poenitentiam accedat.</head>
        </div>
        <gap reason="sampling"/>
      </div>
      <gap reason="sampling"/>
      <div type="section" n="1">
        <head type="rubric"><pb n="518"/>CANONUM POENITENTIALIUM LIBER PRIMUS.</head>
        <div type="chapter" n="1">
          <head type="number">CAPUT PRIMUM.</head>
          <head type="rubric">Quod nulli sit in morte ultima poenitentia deneganda.</head>
          <p>Agnouimus enim poenitentiam morientibus denegari, nec illorum desideriis annui, qui obitus sui tempore hoc
            animae suae cupiunt remedio subueniri. <gap reason="sampling"/> cum Deus ad subueniendum sit paratissimus,
            et inuitans ad poenitentiam sic promittat: <quote source="cf_EZE_33_12">Peccator</quote>, inquit, <quote
              source="cf_EZE_33_12">quacumque die conuersus fuerit, peccata eius non reputabuntur ei.</quote> Et
            iterum: <quote source="cf_EZE_18_32">Nolo mortem peccatoris, sed tantum ut conuertatur et uiuat.</quote>
            <gap reason="sampling"/></p>
          <note type="source" source="D.CEL-0428-369"/>
          <note type="source">Coelestini Papae I. Epist. 2. ad Episcopos prouinciae Uiennensis et Narbonensis, cap.
            2.</note>
        </div>
        <gap reason="sampling"/>
      </div>
